# Code of Conduct

## Our Pledge

We pledge to make participation in our project a welcoming and respectful experience for everyone. We are committed to creating an environment where everyone can contribute freely and safely.

## Our Standards

Examples of positive behavior include:

* Being respectful and considerate of others.
* Welcoming different opinions and experiences.
* Giving and accepting constructive feedback.
* Focusing on what is best for the project and community.
* Showing empathy toward other contributors.

Unacceptable behavior includes harassment, discrimination, personal attacks, insulting comments, and any conduct that makes others feel unsafe or unwelcome.

## Enforcement Responsibilities

Project maintainers are responsible for clarifying and enforcing the standards of this Code of Conduct. They may take appropriate action when unacceptable behavior is reported.

## Scope

This Code of Conduct applies to all project spaces, including the repository, issues, pull requests, discussions, and other project-related interactions.

## Enforcement

Instances of unacceptable behavior may be reported to the project maintainers. Reports will be reviewed fairly and handled appropriately.

## Enforcement Guidelines

Project maintainers may take actions such as a warning, temporary restriction, or removal from project activities depending on the seriousness and circumstances of the violation.

## Attribution

This Code of Conduct is based on the Contributor Covenant and has been adapted for this project.
